        <mxCell id="ht" value="Why the box-equality contract still holds (attachment-strip.spec FM2, no re-pin)" style="text;html=1;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="270" width="700" height="26" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="hb" value="· the placeholder and the settled card render the SAME bytes — only `state` differs (uploading vs done), and the 上传中 badge is absolutely positioned so it never adds a line&#10;· the card root is borderless: with the primitive's 1px frame the root box would be 2px larger than the trigger box the settled card measures through — border-0 makes root box ≡ trigger box&#10;· .spec-chip family classes survive as zero-rule hooks on the trigger, so spec-brief-card's a.spec-chip / img.spec-chip-img and chief-composer-tools' .spec-chip locators keep working unchanged" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=4;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
